    {
        "content": "<p>I just encountered this and spent a while debugging it, because the default value for a proof field accidentally ended up depending on itself and I couldn't get Lean to fill in the default value.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Fields missing: `x`</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Add missing fields:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">   ̲x̲ ̲:̲=̲ ̲_̲ ̲</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: { } : Bar</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Should there be at least some kind of warning when this happens?</p>",
        "id": 578014370,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772980604
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's amusing.</p>\n<p>A reason <code>structure</code> allows this at all is that children structures can make the default values depend on each other. That way you can give some subset of fields and have the others become defined in terms of the others.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In principle there's nothing special about a field default defined in terms of itself, but it's certainly never going to be usable.</p>\n<p>The <code>structure</code> command ought to let you know at definition time.</p>\n<p>It probably also should elaborate the default value using a local context where <code>x</code> is not present! It's way too easy for tactic proofs to pull in values of the local context unnecessarily.</p>",
        "id": 578015670,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1772981923
    }
]